    :schema.property/url "https://schema.org/BusStop"}},
  :schema.class/TouristDestination
  {:block/title "TouristDestination",
   :build/class-properties
   [:schema.property/touristType :schema.property/includesAttraction],
   :build/class-extends [:schema.class/Place],
   :build/properties
   {:logseq.property/icon {:id "camera", :type :emoji},
    :logseq.property/description
    "A tourist destination. In principle any [Place](https://schema.org/Place) can be a [TouristDestination](https://schema.org/TouristDestination) from a [City](https://schema.org/City), Region or [Country](https://schema.org/Country) to an [AmusementPark](https://schema.org/AmusementPark) or [Hotel](https://schema.org/Hotel). This Type can be used on its own to describe a general [TouristDestination](https://schema.org/TouristDestination), or be used as an [additionalType](https://schema.org/additionalType) to add tourist relevant properties to any other [Place](https://schema.org/Place). A [TouristDestination](https://schema.org/TouristDestination) is defined as a [Place](https://schema.org/Place) that contains, or is colocated with, one or more [TouristAttraction](https://schema.org/TouristAttraction)s, often linked by a similar theme or interest to a particular [touristType](https://schema.org/touristType). The [UNWTO](http://www2.unwto.org/) defines Destination (main destination of a tourism trip) as the place visited that is central to the decision to take the trip.",
    :schema.property/url "https://schema.org/TouristDestination"}},
  :schema.class/Airport
